config FREETZ_PACKAGE_MATTER_BRIDGE
	bool "matter-bridge 0.1 (native Matter controller for Domoticz)"
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_1_0_58_MIN
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_IPV6_SUPPORT
	select FREETZ_LIB_libpthread if FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_HAS_multiple_libs
	select FREETZ_LIB_librt if FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_HAS_multiple_libs
	default n
	help
		Native Rust/rs-matter controller and WebSocket JSON server in one
		daemon. Domoticz connects to 127.0.0.1:5580 using its Matter hardware
		driver. No Node.js, Python server or external controller is required.

		For the local freetz-matter accessory, commissioning is automatic
		when its commissioning window is open. Run matter-bridge-setup to
		enable and start both services, then add Matter hardware in Domoticz
		with host 127.0.0.1, port 5580. Run modsave after commissioning.

		The controller persists its fabric, reads real attributes, subscribes
		to reports and sends OnOff/LevelControl commands over CASE.
		This is a known-address, already-networked-device controller, not
		a full python-matter-server replacement or certified Matter product.
		Multicast discovery, Wi-Fi/Thread provisioning and verified Device
		Attestation are not implemented. Test attestation is accepted only
		for loopback by default; remote use requires explicit opt-in.

		The WebSocket API binds to loopback and has no authentication.
		Do not expose it to an untrusted network. Fabric keys and nodes
		live in /tmp/flash/matter-bridge; back up both controller and device
		stores before upgrading firmware.

		Building requires Rust nightly and substantial RAM; builds are
		serialized. matter-bridge-ctl is a standalone diagnostic tool,
		not a second service required by Domoticz.
		See docs/make/matter-bridge.md for scope and verification.

		Can be externalized: /usr/bin/matter-bridge and
		/usr/bin/matter-bridge-ctl. Init/config/fabric remain on the box.